# Plotina-Patch: matrix-js-sdk carries upstream fix #5522.
# Plotina-Marker: no delayed leave event is scheduled
# Plotina-Note: the pin lives in two files, package.json and pnpm-lock.yaml, and the marker
#   cannot live in either of them: a lockfile string is not runtime code. So this patch also
#   writes the marker into public/plotina-patches/0008-js-sdk-5522.txt, which the bundle carries
#   verbatim, and build.py separately asserts the same string is inside assets/index-*.js --
#   it is the warning #5522 adds to MembershipManager.updateExpiryOnJoinedEvent, so seeing it in
#   the bundle's own JS is seeing the fix, not a receipt.
#
# Upstream: matrix-org/matrix-js-sdk #5522, "MatrixRTC: restart the delayed leave event before
#   extending a membership's expiry", merged 2026-09-22, commit
#   6bc94c04aaf6424345dcd5e613cc7e6805cd9c72 (released as v42.3.0). 44 commits after the
#   24929be0 (v42.2.0) our v0.26.1 tag pinned.
# Generated with pnpm 11.21.0 (`pnpm install --lockfile-only`) against upstream element-call
#   v0.26.1, so the lock's integrity hashes are the ones pnpm itself records.
#
# What the fix does, in one line: before extending a membership's `expires`, restart its delayed
#   leave event, and treat a 404 as "the server already sent the leave" (rejoin from scratch)
#   instead of re-sending the membership alone -- that re-send is the ghost with no delayed leave
#   behind it that nothing could then delete.

